// ==UserScript==
// @name         RO Plugin v3 — Rocache
// @namespace    robrowser
// @version      1.2.0-a.36
// @description  Persistent asset cache for the roBrowser asset server (ROConfig.remoteClient), built on fetch interception : the native plugin manager's fetch-intercept lib (needs ROConfig.fetchIntercept on) or the userscript Framework.fetchIntercept (since framework 3.10.0-a.13). Three pluggable storage backends behind a unified interface : `opfs` (OPFS SyncAccessHandle, fastest), `cacheapi` (universal Cache Storage, S2 path), `fs` (Chromium-only legacy webkitRequestFileSystem with ETag sidecar). Cascade default `opfs > cacheapi > fs` ; `/rocache` UI radio lets the user pick + auto-detects capability per browser. Per-file freshness via cyro's Express ETag (If-None-Match) ; default mode `async` revalidates in background with a 1h throttle ; `strict` races a 100ms conditional GET. Invalidation is a manual user action via /rocache → Invalidate cache. NEW in 1.2 : « Bulk download » button pre-populates the active backend with a curated pre-re asset list (~3.8 GB, ~34k files) hosted on catbox.moe, fetched once + cached in IndexedDB. Worker-side orchestrator with capped concurrency (default 10, 1-32), per-attempt 30s timeout, 3 retries with exponential backoff on 5xx/network/timeout (no retry on 4xx — known combo-probe noise). Visible progress bar + pause/resume/cancel. On install, sets `localStorage.RO_DISABLE_FILESYSTEM=1` so the host hides the bundle's FileSystem at boot (the userscript framework patches FileSystem.js `_available` ; the native manager starts its asset worker as `nofs`) — the bundle then goes through `fetch()` for every asset (Firefox path) while `webkitRequestFileSystem*` stay available on the worker for the `fs` backend. Reload required after install for the patch to take effect. On uninstall the flag is cleared, FileSystem comes back on the next reload. Backend switches don't migrate data (out of scope, deferred to a later session). Settings persist in localStorage.rocache_settings and propagate to the asset worker via __RO_setConfig.
// @match        *://*.cyro.live/*
// @match        *://cyro.live/*
// @run-at       document-start
// @grant        unsafeWindow
// @updateURL    https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/meitogi/ro-plugins@main/rocache/1.2.0-a.36/rocache.user.js
// @downloadURL  https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/meitogi/ro-plugins@main/rocache/1.2.0-a.36/rocache.user.js
// ==/UserScript==

